              "pedagogicalTier": "🏛️ PREGUNTA OFICIAL CEPREUNSA • DEDUCCIÓN ANALÍTICA",
              "explanation": "The correct answer is letter C.\nThird paragraph says: “Don’t use your phone in class,”\nwhich is a negative imperative.\n24.What can we infer about the person?\nA. The person likes staying at home all day.\nB. The person doesn’t like routines.\nC. The person likes being active during the day.\nD. The person only studies at night.\nE. The person hates music.\nSOLUCIÓN\nThe correct answer is letter C.\nThe person exercises, studies, and follows a routine, so\nwe infer an active lifestyle.\nRespuesta correcta: C✔\n25.What is the main purpose of the text?\nA. To describe a job.\nB. To explain a school rule.\nC. To talk about a family.\nD. To describe a city.\nE. To give instructions for a daily routine.\nSOLUCIÓN\nThe correct answer is letter E.\nThe text uses imperatives and connectors to guide a daily\nroutine step by step.\nRespuesta correcta: E✔\nTEXT 2\nVideo Games and Discipline\nLucas is a 17-year-old student who loves playing\nvideo games. Every day, he finishes school and goes\nhome to play online with his friends. He usually plays\nfor many hours, and he often forgets about his\nhomework. He likes winning games, and he enjoys\nspending time in virtual worlds, but his grades are\ngetting worse.\nOne afternoon, his teacher talks to him and says:\n“Think about your future and organize your time.”\nLucas feels worried because he wants to enter\nuniversity. So, he decides to change his habits.\nNow, he studies first and finishes his homework\nbefore playing. He sets a time limit, so he only plays\nfor one hour. He doesn’t play late at night, and he\n\nsleeps earlier. He also exercises because he wants to\nfeel more active.\nFollow these tips if you like video games:\n- Play, but control your time.\n- Do your responsibilities first, so you can enjoy\nyour free time.\n- Don’t play all night because you need rest.\n- Be responsible and stay focused on your goals.\nLucas still likes playing video games, but now he has\nbalance in his life and feels more confident about his\nfuture.\nGlossary\n• Grades: a system of classification,\nmeasurement, or quality ranking.\n(calificaciones)\n• Set: refers to placing or fixing something into a\nspecific state. (establecer)\n• Tips: a small, practical piece of information or\nadvice. (sugerencia)\n• Virtual worlds: is a computer-simulated,\npersistent environment where multiple users\ncan interact simultaneously through digital\nrepresentations called avatars. (Mundos\nvirtuales)\n26.What does Lucas usually do after school?\nA. He studies at the library.\nB. He plays video games.\nC. He visits his teacher.\nD. He exercises.\nE. He cooks dinner.\nSOLUCIÓN\nThe correct answer is letter B.\nAccording to the first paragraph, Lucas goes home and\nplays video games after school.\nRespuesta correcta: B✔\n27.Why does Lucas decide to change his habits?\nA. Because he is bored.\nB. Because his friends stop playing.\nC. Because he wants a better future.\nD. Because he changes school.\nE. Because he travels.\nSOLUCIÓN\nThe correct answer is letter C.\nAccording to the second paragraph, He wants to enter\nuniversity, so he changes his routine.\nRespuesta correcta: C✔\n28.What does Lucas do before playing now?\nA. He sleeps\nB. He studies and does homework.\nC. He watches videos\nD. He calls friends\nE. He eats snacks\nSOLUCIÓN\nThe correct answer is letter B.\nAccording to the third paragraph, he studies and finishes\nhomework first\nRespuesta correcta: B✔\n29.Which sentence is the tip that the teacher advice\nfor Lucas?\nA. You should spend more time playing video\ngames.\nB. You must buy a better video game.\nC. Studying is important when you're at\nuniversity.\nD. Don’t play all night because you need rest.\nE. Before doing homework, play video games for\na while.\nSOLUCIÓN\nThe correct answer is letter D.\nAccording to the tips, he shouldn't play all night because he\nneeds to rest.\nRespuesta correcta: D✔\n30.What is the main message of the text?\nA. University is easy.\nB. Discipline helps achieve goals.\nC. Students don’t need rest.\nD. Studying is boring.\nE. Teachers are strict.\nSOLUCIÓN\nThe correct answer is letter B.\nThe text emphasizes discipline and effort to reach goals.\nRespuesta correcta: B✔",
