              "explanation": "The correct answer is letter B\nThe sentences use contrast clues like “isn’t” and\n“but”, meaning you must fill the blanks with the\nantonyms (opposites) if the words “young,\nhardworking and handsome”\n- The opposite of young is old.\n- The opposite of hardworking is lazy.\n- The opposite of handsome is ugly.\nSOLUCIÓN\nThe correct answer is letter D\nThe verb “believe” is used to give opinion and\nfollowed directly by a full clause with a connector (\nthat + subject + verb)\nRespuesta correcta: D✔\nSOLUCIÓN\nThe correct answer is letter B\n“In my view” is used to give an opinion about the\nmovie.\nOptions A, C, D and E are incorrect because they are\nused to talk about personal preferences and do not\nfit grammatically before a complete clause in this\ncontext.\nRespuesta correcta: B✔\nSOLUCIÓN\nThe correct answer is letter D\n“Enjoy” is used to talk about preferences and is\ngrammatically followed by a gerund verb (listening).\nOptions A, B, C and E are expressions used to give\nopinions, not preferences, and do not fit the\nsentence structure.\nRespuesta correcta: D✔\n\nTEXT 1\nTouring Capital Cities\nBy: Andrés Lovón Román\nEmma: I really want to visit Europe this summer. I’m\nlooking at London, Berlin, and Paris, but I can’t\ndecide.\nRyan: I think London is the most exciting city of the\nthree. There are so many museums, theaters, and\nfamous places. Right now, my cousin is studying\nthere, and she says the city is always busy.\nEmma: That’s true, but London is also more\nexpensive than Berlin. Hotels and restaurants cost a\nlot there. I prefer cities that are a little cheaper.\nRyan: Berlin is definitely cheaper, and it’s also quieter\nthan London. People say transportation is easier\nthere too. My brother is visiting Berlin this month,\nand he loves the modern art galleries.\nEmma: I like art, but Paris sounds more romantic to\nme. The cafés are beautiful, and the Eiffel Tower is\nprobably the most famous landmark in Europe.\nRyan: Paris is amazing, but some tourists think the\npeople there are less friendly than in Berlin.\nPersonally, I prefer Berlin because it feels more\nrelaxed.\nEmma: Really? I think Paris has the best food. French\npastries are better than German desserts in my\nopinion.\nRyan: Maybe, but Berlin has more parks and bigger\nstreets. London, however, has the most international\natmosphere. You hear many languages everywhere.\nEmma: Right now, I’m watching travel vlogs about all\nthree cities, and honestly, each one looks incredible.\nParis looks more chic, Berlin looks more modern, and\nLondon looks more energetic.\nRyan: So, which city do you want to visit first?\nEmma: I think\nParis is my first choice, but Berlin is a close second.\nGlossary\n• Busy: full of activity or people\n(ocupado/concurrido).\n• Chic: stylish and fashionable (elegante/con\nestilo).\n• Everywhere: in all places (en todas partes).\n• Landmark: a famous place or monument\n(monumento famoso).\n• Pastries: sweet baked foods like croissants or\ncakes (pasteles).\n• Vlog: a video blog where people share\nexperiences online (videoblog).",
